% composition-series: Ontario Listening Bridges — set 1
% composition-grade: 8
% composition-elements: polyphonic texture made by a two-part interlock: Line A on the beats and Line B in the off-beat gaps, so neither part plays the whole tune and together they make one continuous eighth-note line (bars 3-6); layered form in five stages: one line (bars 1-2), the interlock (3-4), the roles swapped so Line B takes the beats (5-6), thinned to one line with an improvised layer (7), both lines closing an octave apart on C (8); shared punctuation where both lines land on one note (bars 4, 6 and 8); C pentatonic on equal-tempered classroom barred instruments, compared with the reference's bronze ensemble timbre; arranging for two groups; constrained group improvisation in bar 7
% composition-listen: I Nyoman Windha — "Puspanjali" (1989), music for gamelan gong kebyar for the welcome dance of the same name; a specific authorized recording has not yet been selected
% composition-listen-url: https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=I+Nyoman+Windha+Puspanjali+gamelan
% composition-bridge: Hear coordinated interlocking parts, sectional contrast, paired tuning shimmer and large-scale punctuation.
% composition-context: Balinese gamelan composition is a living, changing art with ensemble-specific tuning and rehearsal practice. This equal-tempered classroom polyphony is not gamelan and does not reproduce kotekan.
% composition-distance: Original notes and sectional plan; no Windha passage, tuning, interlocking pattern or gong structure is copied.
